---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Solutions and Improvements handles information sent through the website’s consultation form."
  path="/privacy"
  draftNote="Draft privacy note. Confirm the email provider, retention period and any analytics before launch."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <span class="kicker">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy note</h1>
      <p class="lede">What happens to the information you send us through this website.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--white section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>The consultation form asks for your name, an email address and/or phone number, the project city or ZIP code, the type of project and property, a short description, and how you prefer to be contacted.</p>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>We use it to respond to your request and arrange the consultation. We don’t sell it, and we don’t add you to a marketing list.</p>
      <h2>How it’s handled</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The website is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, it processes technical request data such as your IP address, which we use to protect the form against abuse.</li>
        <li>Form submissions are sent to our office email through an email delivery service.</li>
        <li>We keep inquiries in our office email for as long as needed to respond and to keep records of our projects.</li>
        <li>The site does not use advertising or analytics cookies.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> or call <a href={company.phoneHref}>{company.phoneDisplay}</a> to ask about, correct or delete the information you sent us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
